      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Sometimes admitting that a system is fundamentally unviable is the damage control step before attempting a complete system wipe. While you cannot patch a kernel that is actively rejecting all updates, delegitimizing the flawed hardware or logic that built it creates the space for reconstruction. It is often only by shutting down the faulty process entirely that a viable alternative can even begin to compile.",
